From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sysfb: clip copied source damage to the destination viewport

The damage iterator rounds fractional source coordinates outward. A 3200-pixel
scanout can therefore receive a 3201-pixel damage rectangle. atomic_update
intersects that rectangle with the destination but passes the original damage
to the blitter, writing beyond the mapped framebuffer on the last row.

Translate damage to destination coordinates before intersecting, then translate
the clipped area back for the source read. This also preserves integer panning.
Observed on Uke during a KWin overview transition with a firmware framebuffer.
The direct trace ends in memcpy_toio through drm_fb_xrgb8888_to_argb8888.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_modeset.c
@@ -353,12 +353,19 @@ void drm_sysfb_plane_helper_atomic_update(struct drm_plane *plane, struct drm_atomic_commit *state)
 	drm_atomic_for_each_plane_damage(&iter, &damage) {
 		struct iosys_map dst = sysfb->fb_addr;
 		struct drm_rect dst_clip = plane_state->dst;
+		struct drm_rect src_clip = damage;
+		int dx = plane_state->dst.x1 - (plane_state->src.x1 >> 16);
+		int dy = plane_state->dst.y1 - (plane_state->src.y1 >> 16);
 
-		if (!drm_rect_intersect(&dst_clip, &damage))
+		drm_rect_translate(&src_clip, dx, dy);
+		if (!drm_rect_intersect(&dst_clip, &src_clip))
 			continue;
 
+		src_clip = dst_clip;
+		drm_rect_translate(&src_clip, -dx, -dy);
+
 		iosys_map_incr(&dst, drm_fb_clip_offset(dst_pitch, dst_format, &dst_clip));
-		blit_to_crtc(&dst, &dst_pitch, shadow_plane_state->data, fb, &damage,
+		blit_to_crtc(&dst, &dst_pitch, shadow_plane_state->data, fb, &src_clip,
 			     &shadow_plane_state->fmtcnv_state);
 	}
 
